  "body": "Process change: yes\n\n**Held.** This PR is a trial that the maintainer asked for on 2026-11-18. It has `held-for-merge`. It does not merge until he ends the trial. His words are on the issue.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `.claude/agents/coordinator.md` (new, Fable; Opus if Fable is not available): one long-running agent. It merges, picks issues, dispatches, resolves stuck processes and decides. It writes no code and reads no source.\n- `.claude/agents/context-scout.md` (new, Haiku): a read-only agent. It queries the knowledge graph, searches, reads and writes a context pack with exact paths and line ranges. Four scouts run at all times.\n- `.claude/agents/issue-worker-max.md`, `-high.md`, `-medium.md`: model Opus. `issue-worker-low.md`: model Sonnet. Each worker gets its context from a scout.\n- `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`: new section 1a \"Context comes from a scout\", with a fallback when no scout answers. The report names each search that the worker did itself.\n- `AGENTS.md`: new section \"Agent roles (trial, #2464)\" under the Autonomous Work Law. \"Who works it\" names the coordinator.\n- `docs/decisions/2464-agent-roles-trial.md`: the choices taken unattended.\n\nThe main session keeps the user: reports, questions and maintainer decisions.\n\n## Readings\n\nNo code changed. No build ran. No file under `xtask/` or `scripts/` cites the changed lines.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No coordinator ran from these files before this PR opened.\n- It is not known if a subagent coordinator can start and message its own subagents in each client.\n- The cost of four idle scouts against the reads that they save is not measured. The trial measures it.\n\n`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is not changed.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2464\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
